A51: one cluster (one pset) for all eight cores.

0115 routes A5XELTE through the HAS_CLUSTER topology path, which derives the
cluster from MPIDR. On the A51 the A73s (MPIDR 0x100-0x103, Aff1 = 1) then
become cluster 1 with their own processor set, and this non-AMP scheduler
panics on pset0's ticket lock ("Ticket lock ... is unexpectedly owned by
thread", lck_ticket_contended) as soon as cpus >= 5, even before any A73 is
started. cpus=2 and cpus=4 (A53 cluster only) boot cleanly into iOS.

SWEET (A55+A76) and HEROLTE (A53+Mongoose) run eight cores with the stock
non-cluster path, where every core is CLUSTER_TYPE_SMP cluster 0. Do the same
for the A51; A5XELTE boards other than the A51 keep 0115's behaviour.

diff --git a/osfmk/arm64/machine_routines.c b/osfmk/arm64/machine_routines.c
index 6d56a33..8b6dbf1 100644
--- a/osfmk/arm64/machine_routines.c
+++ b/osfmk/arm64/machine_routines.c
@@ -1050,7 +1050,13 @@ ml_parse_cpu_topology(void)
 		 * on the value provided by EDT. Instead, use the MPIDR value to see if we have
 		 * seen this exact cluster before. If so, then reuse that cluster ID for this CPU.
 		 */
-#if HAS_CLUSTER || defined(A5XELTE)
+		/*
+		 * A51: one cluster (one pset) for all eight cores, like the SWEET and
+		 * HEROLTE 8-core configurations. With the A73s (MPIDR Aff1 = 1) as a
+		 * second pset this non-AMP scheduler panics on pset0's ticket lock
+		 * ("unexpectedly owned") as soon as cpus >= 5 (boots 17b, 21, 22).
+		 */
+#if HAS_CLUSTER || (defined(A5XELTE) && !defined(A51))
 		uint32_t phys_cluster_id = MPIDR_CLUSTER_ID(cpu->phys_id);
 #else
 		uint32_t phys_cluster_id = (cpu->cluster_type == CLUSTER_TYPE_P);
@@ -1084,7 +1090,7 @@ ml_parse_cpu_topology(void)
 			ml_read_reg_range(child, "cpm-impl-reg", &cluster->cpm_IMPL_pa, &cluster->cpm_IMPL_len);
 		}
 
-#if HAS_CLUSTER || defined(A5XELTE)
+#if HAS_CLUSTER || (defined(A5XELTE) && !defined(A51))
 		if (MPIDR_CPU_ID(cpu->phys_id) > cluster_max_cpu_phys_id[phys_cluster_id]) {
 			cluster_max_cpu_phys_id[phys_cluster_id] = MPIDR_CPU_ID(cpu->phys_id);
 		}
@@ -1110,7 +1116,7 @@ ml_parse_cpu_topology(void)
 
 	}
 
